{
  "0": "Training strategy: multiply the current learning rate by 0.7 across all four datasets, leaving other training settings unchanged. Smaller updates may reduce the validation oscillation and early overfitting visible in Electronics while preserving learning in the stronger categories. Preserve the model, features, scoring, loss, seeds, epoch cap of 200 and one trained checkpoint per category.",
  "1": "Sequence modeling: reduce the current maximum causal history length to max(1, floor(0.75 * current_length)), retaining the most recent interactions in chronological order. Removing older context may reduce stale-interest interference and recurrent computation. Apply identical truncation in training and the generated predictor across all four datasets; preserve embeddings, GRU topology, readout, loss and optimizer.",
  "2": "Learning objective: retain the current loss and add 0.03 times the mean softplus(s_negative - s_positive) over valid targets and the existing sampled negatives. The previous 0.1 auxiliary term fell below the incumbent; a smaller coefficient may improve ranking margins with less disruption to the original objective. Apply across all four datasets without changing sampling, scoring, architecture or training settings.",
  "3": "Interest aggregation: replace the current readout with 0.9 times the last valid GRU state plus 0.1 times an exponentially recency-weighted mean of valid GRU states, using a half-life of five interactions. This modest pooled contribution may stabilize noisy final states while keeping recent intent dominant. Apply across all four datasets and update the predictor writer; preserve history selection, embeddings, GRU topology, scoring, loss and optimizer."
}
